(910391, 104725, 26646, '<td valign="top">unique and interesting thought.</td>', 'unique and interesting thought.', '2004-09-15 01:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(910603, 105002, 8054, '<td valign="top">Very nice composition and excellent focus all across the feather (especially in the downy part). The part of the photo that gets serious negative points; color balance. It''s WAY too red. You can see the tint everywhere.</td>', 'Very nice composition and excellent focus all across the feather (especially in the downy part). The part of the photo that gets serious negative points; color balance. It''s WAY too red. You can see the tint everywhere.', '2004-09-15 03:44:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(910612, 105137, 8054, '<td valign="top">Love the creativity shown here. Colors are very vivid and well saturated. But for some reason, I get dizzy trying to focus on this image. There doesn''t appear to be a main focal point and in some areas I actually see double.</td>', 'Love the creativity shown here. Colors are very vivid and well saturated. But for some reason, I get dizzy trying to focus on this image. There doesn''t appear to be a main focal point and in some areas I actually see double.', '2004-09-15 03:46:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(910624, 104862, 8054, '<td valign="top">Another very creative photo in this challenge. The most difficult part is taking the photo without a trace of the camera or photographer. Sorry, but I can see both in your entry.</td>', 'Another very creative photo in this challenge. The most difficult part is taking the photo without a trace of the camera or photographer. Sorry, but I can see both in your entry.', '2004-09-15 03:48:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(910696, 104860, 8054, '<td valign="top">I don''t think the shallow DOF works to your advantage here. If the snail was facing the camera and shallow DOF was applied to blur part of the shell would look much nicer. Exposure is a bit dark. Good use of negative space in front of the snail.</td>', 'I don''t think the shallow DOF works to your advantage here. If the snail was facing the camera and shallow DOF was applied to blur part of the shell would look much nicer. Exposure is a bit dark. Good use of negative space in front of the snail.', '2004-09-15 03:57:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(910697, 104513, 8054, '<td valign="top">Interesting composition is flawed by harsh and direct flash lighting. If this is an external flash, try using  bounce/fill flash if possible. Or try a softbox. Short of that, try some kleenex in front of the flash to help diffuse and soften the light.</td>', 'Interesting composition is flawed by harsh and direct flash lighting. If this is an external flash, try using  bounce/fill flash if possible. Or try a softbox. Short of that, try some kleenex in front of the flash to help diffuse and soften the light.', '2004-09-15 04:00:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(910699, 105020, 8054, '<td valign="top">Oh man, this one made me laugh out loud! Big bug eyes! Great creativity and use of selective desat. My sole complaint is the model''s forehead as it''s slightly overexposed. 7</td>', 'Oh man, this one made me laugh out loud! Big bug eyes! Great creativity and use of selective desat. My sole complaint is the model''s forehead as it''s slightly overexposed. 7', '2004-09-15 04:02:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(910710, 104795, 8054, '<td valign="top">Great shot! Love the strong contrast of this shot. Those are my favorite type of b/w or duotone shots.  Things I feel are missing are perhaps some ice cubes in the drink and a less distracting reflection on the right. The reflections of the glass are very interesting but if you want to maximize focus time on the glass, make the most of it. Give the eyes something to look at. I think you had an overhead light source so even a plain reflection would have worked as well or maybe a dark gray to show the drops on the glass surface. And to be really nitpicky, wax the glass surface so the water beads vs spreading. Otherwise, I really enjoyed this photo. Good job! 7</td>', 'Great shot! Love the strong contrast of this shot. Those are my favorite type of b/w or duotone shots.  Things I feel are missing are perhaps some ice cubes in the drink and a less distracting reflection on the right. The reflections of the glass are very interesting but if you want to maximize focus time on the glass, make the most of it. Give the eyes something to look at. I think you had an overhead light source so even a plain reflection would have worked as well or maybe a dark gray to show the drops on the glass surface. And to be really nitpicky, wax the glass surface so the water beads vs spreading. Otherwise, I really enjoyed this photo. Good job! 7', '2004-09-15 04:08:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(910724, 105025, 8054, '<td valign="top">This my favorite of the challenge. The simplicity of the idea is amazing and works very well. Contrast is a bit blown out in the real sky (not reflected sky) but that makes me want to focus more on the mirror and trace the lines. Not that I like overexposed skies but it''s not as distracting here. Plus the frame forces the eye to look there and the color forces the eye even more. A solid 9 but since I love this shot so much, I''ll give it a 10.</td>', 'This my favorite of the challenge. The simplicity of the idea is amazing and works very well. Contrast is a bit blown out in the real sky (not reflected sky) but that makes me want to focus more on the mirror and trace the lines. Not that I like overexposed skies but it''s not as distracting here. Plus the frame forces the eye to look there and the color forces the eye even more. A solid 9 but since I love this shot so much, I''ll give it a 10.', '2004-09-15 04:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(910732, 104342, 8054, '<td valign="top">Looks like the type of scene you see in commercials of people looking for something in the attic and there always seems to be a mirror up there. Model looks very relaxed and is pondering something. Love the duotone and the textures of the floor and hair seem to complement each other very well. Well composed but the upper left corner of the frame seems a bit overexposed. I looked at this a second time and thought about the upper left corner a lot. It gives a nice balance to the opposite corner of the frame and it seems to work well especially since there''s more lighter parts of the frame than darker parts. In my opinion, darker portions would ask for more attention away from the main subject. 9</td>', 'Looks like the type of scene you see in commercials of people looking for something in the attic and there always seems to be a mirror up there. Model looks very relaxed and is pondering something. Love the duotone and the textures of the floor and hair seem to complement each other very well. Well composed but the upper left corner of the frame seems a bit overexposed. I looked at this a second time and thought about the upper left corner a lot. It gives a nice balance to the opposite corner of the frame and it seems to work well especially since there''s more lighter parts of the frame than darker parts. In my opinion, darker portions would ask for more attention away from the main subject. 9', '2004-09-15 04:21:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(910734, 104498, 8054, '<td valign="top">Very cute photo of a horse admiring himself in the mirror. Nice details and composition. Great job of getting the horse to look right into the camera via the mirror, too.</td>', 'Very cute photo of a horse admiring himself in the mirror. Nice details and composition. Great job of getting the horse to look right into the camera via the mirror, too.', '2004-09-15 04:24:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(910752, 104735, 19952, '<td valign="top">Really nice dark photo with excellent patterns and composition. This is one of my faves of the challenge so far. Great job.</td>', 'Really nice dark photo with excellent patterns and composition. This is one of my faves of the challenge so far. Great job.', '2004-09-15 04:32:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(910755, 105021, 19952, '<td valign="top">Really great capture of a eery image with excellent colors and clarity. That really looks like a tail on the right. Nice job!</td>', 'Really great capture of a eery image with excellent colors and clarity. That really looks like a tail on the right. Nice job!', '2004-09-15 04:33:59.000000', NULL, 1),
