(917522, 103808, 19959, '<td valign="top">:-)<br/> <br/>My first top ten... thanks to everyone for their constructive comments...<br/> <br/>A few people have asked how I got the effect:<br/> <br/>I set up and composed for the mirrors and the platform. I fired off some test shots to judge exposure whilst waiting for the train.<br/> <br/>I waited for the train to stop and started the long exposure just before it began moving off. This effectively froze the image of the passenger, as the train moved away it created the motion blur.<br/> <br/>(As for the positioning of the lone passenger in the shot. I got lucky!)<br/> <br/>Regards<br/> <br/>Chris<br/> <br/></td>', ':-) My first top ten... thanks to everyone for their constructive comments... A few people have asked how I got the effect: I set up and composed for the mirrors and the platform. I fired off some test shots to judge exposure whilst waiting for the train. I waited for the train to stop and started the long exposure just before it began moving off. This effectively froze the image of the passenger, as the train moved away it created the motion blur. (As for the positioning of the lone passenger in the shot. I got lucky!) Regards Chris ', '2004-09-20 03:13:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(917538, 105025, 9668, '<td valign="top">I love this shot! Reminds me of <a href="//www.atara.net/magritte/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">René Magritte</a>, something like <a href="//www.atara.net/magritte/30s/human-condition.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this</a> or <a href="//www.atara.net/magritte/40s/call-of-peaks.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this</a>. Awsomely done!</td>', 'I love this shot! Reminds me of René Magritte, something like this or this. Awsomely done!', '2004-09-20 03:20:36.000000', NULL, 0),
