(1151629, 105010, 9581, '<td valign="top">Maybe yellow is the point here but I think if you set your ISO higher it will give you more true colors... Before you take the picture what ever it may be fix your settings like you want for the light adjustments and take a picture of a white sheet of paper if you have the darkest black and gray do them too. then if use photo shop load the white gray and black in and save it in the file mmm uh oh minds gone its curves that help take the tint of yellow and give the photo back or enhances the true white balance in it. <br/> <br/>Ask some of the pros on this I am still playing with this...your photos are looking good..</td>', 'Maybe yellow is the point here but I think if you set your ISO higher it will give you more true colors... Before you take the picture what ever it may be fix your settings like you want for the light adjustments and take a picture of a white sheet of paper if you have the darkest black and gray do them too. then if use photo shop load the white gray and black in and save it in the file mmm uh oh minds gone its curves that help take the tint of yellow and give the photo back or enhances the true white balance in it.  Ask some of the pros on this I am still playing with this...your photos are looking good..', '2005-02-05 05:14:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(1156981, 105037, 12253, '<td valign="top">Skip--I think this would have done better if you had played down the camera.  If you could have held it to the side and captured yourself in a serious pose against the sky.  I think it''s the camera that hurt this; substitute in a beautiful woman in it and it would have been top 10. :)</td>', 'Skip--I think this would have done better if you had played down the camera.  If you could have held it to the side and captured yourself in a serious pose against the sky.  I think it''s the camera that hurt this; substitute in a beautiful woman in it and it would have been top 10. :)', '2005-02-08 09:13:11.000000', NULL, 0),
